THE RULE OF COMPOUND STABILITY
A compound superstructure is only as stable as its most volatile member. If a highly unstable element (like Uranium) is introduced into a compound, the entire alliance risks a critical runaway cascade. Therefore, all compound formulas must be strictly vetted for Authority Density before they are allowed to form.

